## -----------------------------------------------------------------
## Produkt (Product) Service Sub-Profile
## -----------------------------------------------------------------
## ROLE: Describes the NeTEx touchpoints of Entur's fare-product
##       catalogue (FareProducts / tariffs / fare tables). Grounded in
##       the EFIP-style XML export examples: single tickets, carnets
##       (klippekort), zone- and distance-based fares. Pins the master-
##       and route-data references a product delivery carries, and the
##       fare objects it is built from.
##
## STATUS — DEMONSTRATOR, HARMONISED WITH THE NORDIC FARES OVERLAY:
##       No product export/import runs in production yet, so products
##       are not ratified into the Nordic Profile. The fare vocabulary
##       and the NP fare shapes now live in the Nordic fares overlay
##       (netex-nordic-fares.ttl, profile:NP_Fares) — it realises this
##       profile's former PROPOSAL list against the generated base, so
##       every fare class here is a grounded netex: IRI. This sub-profile
##       therefore no longer restates fare shapes: it imports the overlay
##       and declares only the Entur product SERVICE scope (what it
##       consumes / handles) plus any Entur tightening beyond NP.
##
## GPA PLACEMENT — TWO EXPORT VARIANTS (see examples):
##       (A) EFIP-style: each GenericParameterAssignment is wrapped in
##           its own FareStructureElement and referenced from the
##           ValidableElement via FareStructureElementRef.
##       (B) Current solution: GenericParameterAssignments sit inline
##           under validityParameterAssignments on the FSE / product /
##           ValidableElement.
##       Both express the same constraints — only the GPA nesting
##       differs. The NP fare shapes are placement-neutral.
##
## Peer of the other service sub-profiles: imports netex-entur.ttl,
## never another sub-profile. The income model builds on products.
##
## Imports: netex-entur.ttl (Entur governance) → netex-nordic.ttl
##          netex-nordic-fares.ttl (Nordic fares overlay: NP fare shapes)
##          → generated NeTEx base (netex:) + nordic vocab
##
## Generated: 2026-08-12
## -----------------------------------------------------------------

@prefix netex:   <https://netex-cen.eu/ontology#> .
@prefix profile: <https://netex-cen.eu/profile#> .
@prefix entur:   <https://entur.org/ontology#> .
@prefix produkt: <https://entur.org/service/produkt#> .
@prefix sh:      <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

## --- Import Entur governance + Nordic fares overlay ---
<https://entur.org/service/produkt> a owl:Ontology ;
    owl:imports <https://entur.org/ontology> ,
                <https://netex-cen.eu/profile/nordic/fares> .

## =================================================================
## SERVICE DEFINITION
## =================================================================

produkt:ProductService a entur:SubProfile ;
    rdfs:label "Produkt — Product Service Profile" ;
    skos:definition "Sub-profile for the fare-product catalogue (fare products, tariffs, fare tables). Builds on the Nordic fares overlay (NP_Fares); demonstrator only — no production I/O yet." ;
    entur:basedOn profile:NP_Fares .

## =================================================================
## CONSUMED REFERENCES (master + route data a product points at)
## =================================================================
## Every example anchors its fare product to organisation and zone/
## route data by @ref. These are the dependencies to route/master data
## the request asks us to make explicit. Property IRIs follow the base's
## shared lowerCamelCase reference style (as in the other sub-profiles);
## the owning class is carried by the generated restrictions.
##
## NOTE: examples contain SYNTHETIC ids (e.g. NOR:FareZone:*,
## INN:Authority:INN_ID) that need not resolve in Entur's databases —
## so reference targets below are documented, not hard-required.
## -----------------------------------------------------------------

produkt:ProductService produkt:consumes
    ## --- Organisation (ResourceFrame / central registry) ---
    netex:authorityRef ,
    netex:operatorRef ,
    ## --- Fare geography → stop/route data ---
    netex:fareZoneRef ,
    netex:tariffZoneRef ,
    netex:scheduledStopPointRef ,
    ## --- Service scope ---
    netex:lineRef ,
    netex:transportSubmode .

## =================================================================
## OBJECTS IN SCOPE
## =================================================================
## The fare classes this service handles — now all grounded netex: IRIs
## via the Nordic fares overlay — plus the master/route classes the
## products reference.
## -----------------------------------------------------------------

produkt:ProductService produkt:requiresClass
    ## --- Fare products ---
    netex:PreassignedFareProduct ,
    netex:AmountOfPriceUnitProduct ,
    ## --- Fare structure ---
    netex:FareStructureElement ,
    netex:GenericParameterAssignment ,
    netex:ValidableElement ,
    netex:AccessRightInProduct ,
    netex:GeographicalInterval ,
    ## --- Usage parameters (from the example limitations) ---
    netex:UserProfile ,
    netex:CompanionProfile ,
    netex:Refunding ,
    netex:PurchaseWindow ,
    netex:UsageValidityPeriod ,
    netex:FrequencyOfUse ,
    netex:Interchanging ,
    ## --- Pricing grid ---
    netex:FareTable ,
    netex:Cell ,
    netex:FarePrice ,
    netex:TypeOfPricingRule ,
    ## --- Fare geography ---
    netex:FareZone ,
    netex:TariffZone ,
    ## --- Referenced master / route data ---
    netex:Authority ,
    netex:Operator ,
    netex:ScheduledStopPoint ,
    netex:Line .

## =================================================================
## SERVICE-SPECIFIC CONSTRAINTS
## =================================================================
## Fare-object shapes (FareProduct, PreassignedFareProduct,
## FareStructureElement, GenericParameterAssignment, GeographicalInterval,
## FareTable / Cell, UserProfile, Refunding, …) are OWNED by the Nordic
## fares overlay (profile:NP_Fares, netex-nordic-fares.ttl) and are
## placement-neutral for the two GPA variants (A/B, see header). This
## sub-profile imports that overlay and does NOT restate those shapes.
##
## Entur-specific tightening beyond NP is added here only once a real
## product export against resolvable registry data exists. None yet —
## today's example ids are partly synthetic (NOR:FareZone:*,
## INN:Authority:INN_ID), so hard cross-reference class checks are
## deferred, mirroring the overlay's FUTURE PROFILING section:
##   - GeographicalInterval[IntervalType=tariffZone] → FareZone
##   - FareZone.members → ScheduledStopPoint      (fare geography ↔ stops)
##   - AuthorityRef / OperatorRef → Organisation   (central registry)
##   - product / ValidableElement → TransportSubmode / Line (service scope)
## StartTimeAtStopPoint → ScheduledStopPoint is already tied 1:1 in NP.

## =================================================================
## END OF PRODUCT SERVICE PROFILE
## =================================================================
